"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both BAC and GS utilize regression analysis to assess hedge effectiveness. BAC uses this method 'at the inception of a hedge and for each reporting period thereafter' to determine if derivatives are highly effective. GS also uses regression analysis but provides specific quantitative thresholds (coefficient of determination of 80% or greater and slope between 80% and 125%) for interest rate swaps to be considered highly effective, whereas BAC's cited text mentions the use of regression but does not specify numerical effectiveness thresholds in the same sentence.",
