"comparison": "Both BAC and JPM define the condition for discontinuing hedge accounting based on effectiveness. BAC states it discontinues hedge accounting 'when it is determined that a derivative is not expected to be or has ceased to be highly effective,' which is substantively similar to JPM's statement that 'hedge accounting is discontinued' if 'a derivative is not highly effective.' Both disclosures focus on the loss of effectiveness as the trigger for de-designation.",
